  "type": "multipleCorrect",
  "level": 3,
  "question": {
    "text": "<p>In the circuit shown, <math><mi>L</mi><mtext> </mtext><mo>=</mo><mtext> </mtext><mn>1</mn><mtext> </mtext><mtext>μ</mtext><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext> </mtext><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mtext> </mtext><mtext>μ</mtext><mi>F</mi><mtext> </mtext><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>d</mi><mtext> </mtext><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mtext> </mtext><mi>k</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi><mo>.</mo><mtext> </mtext></math> They are connected in series with an a.c. source <math><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mi>V</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mtext> </mtext><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">sin</mi></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mtext>ω</mtext><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></math> as shown. Which of the following options is/are correct?<br ><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/skflzdeounqrjeglmncmnzywmskplktgavkdxirnucfvacbvku.jpeg\"/></p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "fyr8X",
      "text": "At  <math><mi>ω</mi><mo>≫</mo><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup><mi> </mi><mi>r</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>d</mi><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">sec</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi> </mi></mrow></mrow></math> the circuit behaves as a capacitor",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "nCwpN",
      "text": "The frequency at which the current will be in phase with the voltage is independent of <math><mi>R</mi></math>",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "nGjh3",
      "text": "The current will be in phase with the voltage if  <math><mi>ω</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mi> </mi><mi>r</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>d</mi><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">sec</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi> </mi></mrow></mrow></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "DGLFP",
      "text": "At <math><mi>&omega;</mi><mo>~</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>&nbsp;</mi></math> the current flowing through the circuit becomes nearly zero",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The current will be&nbsp;in phase with voltage when phase angle is zero,&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mi>tan</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo><mtext>&#981;</mtext><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mtext>&#969;</mtext><mi>L</mi><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mtext>&#969;</mtext><mi>C</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mi>R</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>Where&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtext>&#969;</mtext><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>R</mi></math>&nbsp;are the angular frequency, inductance, capacitance and resistance respectively.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mtext>&#969;</mtext><mo>=</mo><msub><mtext>&#969;</mtext><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mi>L</mi><mi>C</mi></msqrt></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mtext>&#969;</mtext><mtext>&#959;</mtext></msub></math>is independent of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>r</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>f</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>q</mi><mi>u</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>c</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mtext>&#969;</mtext><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>6</mn></msup><mtext>&#160;</mtext><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mo>/</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math></p><p>Current in the circuit is given by,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><msqrt><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mtext>&#969;</mtext><mi>L</mi><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mtext>&#969;</mtext><mi>C</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></msqrt></mfrac></math></p><p>When&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtext>&#969;</mtext><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mtext>&#160;</mtext><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>For&nbsp;&nbsp;<math><mtext>&#969;</mtext><mo>&#8811;</mo><msub><mrow><mtext>&#969;</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></math>&nbsp;circuit behaves as inductor.</p>",
    "image": null
  },
